  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Given an array CCC of MMM integers and a square matrix AAA (with integer entries) of dimension N×NN \\times NN×N, verify whether the following equation is true,\n\nC0IN+C1A+C2A2+…CM−1AM−1≡0N(mod998244353)C_0 I_{N} + C_1 A + C_2 A^2 + \\dots C_{M-1} A^{M-1}  \\equiv 0_N \\pmod{998244353}C0​IN​+C1​A+C2​A2+…CM−1​AM−1≡0N​(mod998244353)\n\nwhere 0N0_N0N​ is the square null matrix (matrix in which all elements are zero) and INI_NIN​ is the identity matrix, both having dimensions N×NN \\times NN×N.\n\n**Note:**\n\n\nTwo matrices A,BA, BA,B each with integer entries are said to be congruent modulo MMM iff all entries of A−BA - BA−B are divisible by MMM. This is denoted as A≡B(modM)A \\equiv B \\pmod{M}A≡B(modM).\nSince the input-output is large, prefer using fast input-output methods.\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line contains TTT denoting the number of test cases. Then the test cases follow.\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer MMM denoting the length of CCC.\nThe second line of each testcase contains MMM space separated integers, C0,C1,…CM−1C_0, C_1, \\dots C_{M-1}C0​,C1​,…CM−1​ representing the array CCC.\nThe third line of each testcase contains a single integer NNN denoting the size of the square matrix AAA.\nThe iii-th line of the next NNN lines contains NNN space-separated integers Ai,1,Ai,2,…,Ai,NA_{i,1}, A_{i,2}, \\dots, A_{i,N}Ai,1​,Ai,2​,…,Ai,N​ denoting the elements of the iii-th row of the matrix AAA.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a single line `YES` if the equation C0In+C1A+C2A2+…CM−1AM−1≡0N(mod998244353)C_0 I_n + C_1 A + C_2 A^2 + \\dots C_{M-1} A^{M-1}  \\equiv 0_N \\pmod{998244353}C0​In​+C1​A+C2​A2+…CM−1​AM−1≡0N​(mod998244353) satisfies, and `NO` otherwise.\n\n\nOutput is **case insensitive**, i.e., you may print each character of the string in uppercase or lowercase (for example, the strings \"yEs\", \"yes\", \"Yes\" and \"YES\" will all be treated as identical).",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤2001 \\leq T \\leq 2001≤T≤200",
      "1≤N≤10001 \\leq N \\leq 10001≤N≤1000",
      "1≤M≤111 \\leq M \\leq 111≤M≤11",
      "0≤Ci&lt;9982443530 \\leq C_i \\lt 9982443530≤Ci​&lt;998244353",
      "0≤Ai,j&lt;9982443530 \\leq A_{i,j} \\lt 9982443530≤Ai,j​&lt;998244353",
      "Sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 200020002000.",
      "Subtasks",
      "**Subtask 1 (100 points):** Original constraints"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n3\n998244351 998244348 1\n2\n1 2\n3 4\n3\n998244351 998244348 1\n2\n1 1\n1 1",
        "output": "YES\nNO",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nBoth test cases have the same co-efficients. Since 998244351≡−2(mod998244353)998244351 \\equiv -2 \\pmod{998244353}998244351≡−2(mod998244353) and 998244348≡−5(mod998244353)998244348 \\equiv -5 \\pmod{998244353}998244348≡−5(mod998244353), for convenience of explanation, we shall take the co-efficients as −2,−5,1-2, -5, 1−2,−5,1. Note that this does not affect the answer.\nTest case 111: The given matrix, A=[1234]A = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 \\end{bmatrix}A=[13​24​], satisfies the equation −2I2−5A+A2=02-2 I_2 -5 A + A^2 = 0_2−2I2​−5A+A2=02​, so the answer is YES.\nTest case 222: For the given matrix, A=[1111]A = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\end{bmatrix}A=[11​11​], the left hand side of the equation evaluates to, −2I2−5A+A2=[−5−3−3−5]-2I_2 - 5A + A^2 = \\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -3\\\\-3 & -5\\end{bmatrix}−2I2​−5A+A2=[−5−3​−3−5​]. Clearly none of the entries are divisible by 998244353998244353998244353, so the answer is NO."
      }
    ]
  },
